bers in some expression.\n2. Or **to solve the problem** using the given numbers.\n\nIf you want to **calculate 327**, here's a way:\n\n**44 + 60 + 51 = 155**  \n**12 + 91 = 103**  \n**155 + 103 = 258**  \n**258 + 14 = 272**  \n**272 + 12 = 284**  \n\nThis is not 327, but it's close.\n\nLet me know if you'd like a different approach or a specific method!", token_ids=[785, 3491, 7460, 601, 311, 11047, 220, 18, 17, 22, 1667, 678, 315, 279, 5109, 25, 220, 19, 19, 11, 220, 21, 15, 11, 220, 20, 16, 11, 220, 16, 19, 11, 220, 24, 16, 11, 220, 16, 17, 382, 11209, 11, 2474, 3070, 9330, 40975, 311, 3070, 2982, 537, 11625, 279, 3491, 97219, 432, 1035, 387, 2664, 311, 37163, 3425, 498, 8791, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 3070, 35597, 220, 18, 17, 22, 1667, 334, 279, 2661, 5109, 304, 1045, 7493, 624, 17, 13, 2521, 3070, 983, 11625, 279, 3491, 334, 1667, 279, 2661, 5109, 382, 2679, 498, 1366, 311, 3070, 35597, 220, 18, 17, 22, 97219, 1588, 594, 264, 1616, 1447, 334, 19, 19, 488, 220, 21, 15, 488, 220, 20, 16, 284, 220, 16, 20, 20, 334, 2303, 334, 16, 17, 488, 220, 24, 16, 284, 220, 16, 15, 18, 334, 2303, 334, 16, 20, 20, 488, 220, 16, 15, 18, 284, 220, 17, 20, 23, 334, 2303, 334, 17, 20, 23, 488, 220, 16, 19, 284, 220, 17, 22, 17, 334, 2303, 334, 17, 22, 17, 488, 220, 16, 17, 284, 220, 17, 23, 19, 334, 18611, 1986, 374, 537, 220, 18, 17, 22, 11, 714, 432, 594, 3265, 382, 10061, 752, 1414, 421, 498, 4172, 1075, 264, 2155, 5486, 476, 264, 3151, 1714, 0, 151645], routed_experts=None, cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None), CompletionOutput(index=3, text="To calculate 327 using all of the numbers **44, 60, 51, 14, 91, 12**, we need to **find a combination of operations** (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division) that results in 327.\n\n### Let’s try one possible approach:\n\nWe can try grouping some numbers and combining them to get close to 327. For example:\n\n- 91 + 12 = 103  \n- 60 + 51 = 111  \n- 44 + 14 = 58  \n- 327 - (91 + 12 + 60 + 51 + 44 + 14) = 327 - 270 = 57, which doesn't help.\n\nLet’s try another approach:\n\n### Try:\n\n91 + 14 = 105  \n60 + 51 = 111  \n44 + 12 = 56  \nNow try combining the two groups:  \n105 + 111 + 56 = 272 → still not enough.\n\nWhat if we do:\n\n91 + 60 = 151  \n12 + 51 = 63  \n14 + 44 = 58  \nNow add: 151 + 63 = 214 + 58 = 272 again.\n\nStill no. What if we multiply:\n\nTry:  \n(91 + 60) × (14 - 12) = 151 × 2 = 302  \nThen 302 + 51 = 353  \nStill too high.\n\nWhat if we try:\n\n(91 + 12 + 14 + 60) = 185  \n(51 - 44) = 7  \nNow 185 + 7 = 192\n\nNo.\n\nWhat if we try:\n\n(51 × 6) = 306  \nThen 327 - 306 = 21 → so 6 + 21 = 27\n\nBut that's not helpful.\n\nLet me try again:\n\n### Final try:\n\nTry:\n\n91 + 14 = 105  \n60 + 51 = 111  \n12 + 44 = 56  \nNow: 105 + 111 + 56 = 272\n\nStill no. What about:\n\nTry:\n\n60 × 5 = 300  \nThen 327 - 300 = 27 → 27 = 14 + 12 + 1 (non-integer)\n\nNot helpful.\n\nLet me check again:\n\n- 91 + 12 = 103  \n- 60 + 51 = 111  \n- 44 + 14 = 58  \nNow try: 103 + 111 = 214 + 58 = 272 again.\n\nClose.\n\nTry:\n\nTry: (91 + 60 + 51) = 202  \n(14 - 12) = 2  \n202 + 2 = 204\n\nNope.\n\nMaybe:\n\nTry: (91 - 14) = 77  \n(60 - 44) = 16  \nNow 77 + 16 = 93\n\nNo.\n\nIs there a way to use all the numbers in a valid expression?\n\nTry:\n\n(51 × (60 - 91)) = 51 × (-31) = negative  \nNo.\n\nTry:\n\n(12 + 44) × (60 - 51) = 56 × 9 = 504  \nThen 504 + (91 - 14) = 504 + 77 = 581 → too high.\n\nTry:\n\n(12 + 44) × (51 - 91) = 56 × (-40) = -2240 → too low.\n\nTry:\n\n(91 + 60) × (51 - 14) = 151 × 37 = 5607 → way too high.\n\nTry:\n\n(12 × 44) = 528  \n528 - 14 = 514  \n514 - 60 = 454  \n454 - 51 = 403\n\nNo.\n\nFinally, try:\n\n(91 + 60) + (51 + 14) = 151 + 65 = 216  \n216 + 44 = 260  \n260 + 12 = 272\n\nNo. Still not 327.\n\n### Final expression:\n$$\n(91 + 12) + (60 + 51 + 14 + 44) = 103 + 129 = 232\n$$\n\nClose but not 327.\n\nTry:\n\n$$\n(91 + 60) × (51 - 14) = 151 × 37 = 5607\n$$\n\nNo.\n\nIt seems **no valid expression** can be formed with these numbers to exactly get 327.\n\nLet me try one last time:\n\n$$\n(51 × 6) + (91 - 12) = 306 + 79 = 385\n$$\n\nNo.\n\nFinal attempt:\n\n$$\n(91 + 60 + 14) + (51 - 12) = 165 + 39 = 204\n$$\n\nNo.\n\nLet me check if I made a mistake earlier:\n\nWait — what if we do:\n\n(91 × 4) = 364  \nThen 364 - (60 + 51 + 12 + 14) = 364 - 137 = 227\n\nClose.\n\nTry:\n\n(91 × 4) - (60 + 51 + 12 + 14) = 364 - 137 = 227 → not 327.\n\nStill not.\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\nNo valid expression can be formed with the given numbers to exactly calculate 327.", token_ids=[1249, 11047, 220, 18, 17, 22, 1667, 678, 315, 279, 5109, 3070, 19, 19, 11, 220, 21, 15, 11, 220, 20, 16, 11, 220, 16, 19, 11, 220, 24, 16, 11, 220, 16, 17, 97219, 582, 1184, 311, 3070, 3903, 264, 10601, 315, 7525, 334, 320, 718, 680, 11, 75240, 11, 46444, 11, 12804, 8, 429, 3059, 304, 220, 18, 17, 22, 382, 14374, 6771, 748, 1430, 825, 3204, 5486, 1447, 1654, 646, 1430, 49184, 1045, 5109, 323, 34171, 1105, 311, 633, 3265, 311, 220, 18, 17, 22, 13, 1752, 3110, 1447, 12, 220, 24, 16, 488, 220, 16, 17, 284, 220, 16, 15, 18, 2303, 12, 220, 21, 15, 488, 220, 20, 16, 284, 220, 16, 16, 16, 2303, 12, 220, 19, 19, 488, 220, 16, 19, 284, 220, 20, 23, 2303, 12, 220, 18, 17, 22, 481, 320, 24, 16, 488, 220, 16, 17, 488, 220, 21, 15, 488, 220, 20, 16, 488, 220, 19, 19, 488, 220, 16, 19, 8, 284, 220, 18, 17, 22, 481, 220, 17, 22, 15, 284, 220, 20, 22, 11, 892, 3171, 944, 1492, 382, 10061, 748, 1430, 2441, 5486, 1447, 14374, 9735, 1447, 24, 16, 488, 220, 16, 19, 284, 220, 16, 15, 20, 2303, 21, 15, 488, 220, 20, 16, 284, 220, 16, 16, 16, 2303, 19, 19, 488, 220, 16, 17, 284, 220, 20, 21, 2303, 7039, 1430, 34171, 279, 1378, 5203, 25, 2303, 16, 15, 20, 488, 220, 16, 16, 16, 488, 220, 20, 21, 284, 220, 17, 22, 17, 11397, 2058, 537, 3322, 382, 3838, 421, 582, 653, 1447, 24, 16, 488, 220, 21, 15, 284, 220, 16, 20, 16, 2303, 16, 17, 488, 220, 20, 16, 284, 220, 21, 18, 2303, 16, 19, 488, 220, 19, 19, 284, 220, 20, 23, 2303, 7039, 912, 25, 220, 16, 20, 16, 488, 